-- SPIKE: the rule-version axis (tcRuleValidTime) is LOAD-BEARING.
--
-- `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` is a nullary DATE builtin that reads the
-- rule-valid-time axis stamped by `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (and by
-- the per-day interval iterators such as VALUE AT). When the axis is unset,
-- it falls back to the localized current day (same computation as TODAY).
--
-- Rule versioning thereby becomes expressible as ordinary L4: the same
-- predicate, evaluated under two different rule-versions, yields two
-- different results.
--
-- Harness clock: JL4_FIXED_NOW = 2025-01-31T15:45:30Z, so the ambient
-- (unset-axis) fallback day is 2025-01-31, which is on the NEW side of the
-- 2024-01-01 changeover.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

TIMEZONE IS "Etc/UTC"

-- GST rose from 7% to 9% for rules effective on/after 2024-01-01.
`GST rate` MEANS
  IF (DATE_SERIAL `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 1 2024))
  THEN 9
  ELSE 7

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`GST payable on` amount MEANS amount TIMES `GST rate` DIVIDED BY 100

-- expected: 7 — same predicate, OLD rule-version
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) `GST rate`

-- expected: 9 — same predicate, NEW rule-version
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 7 2024) `GST rate`

-- expected: 7 — flips BACK under the old version (WHNFWhen cache
-- revalidation across context switches, not staleness)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) `GST rate`

-- expected: 9 — ambient: axis unset, fallback = localized today 2025-01-31
#EVAL `GST rate`

-- expected: 70 — composes through a dependent rule (old version)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (`GST payable on` 1000)

-- expected: 90 — dependent rule under the new version
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 7 2024) (`GST payable on` 1000)

-- expected: 7 — VALUE AT's per-day UnderRulesEffectiveAt stamp is load-bearing
#EVAL `VALUE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (GIVEN d YIELD `GST rate`)

-- expected: 9
#EVAL `VALUE AT` (Date 1 7 2024) (GIVEN d YIELD `GST rate`)
